# Igor environment -- copy to .env in this same directory and edit.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   chmod 600 .env
#
# bin/tick.sh sources .env from $IGOR_HOME (the repo root) on every
# run. Same file is used for local dev and systemd-managed installs.

# Anthropic API key (NOT the Claude Max OAuth token).
#
# Create in the Anthropic Console (https://console.anthropic.com).
# Use a dedicated key for Igor so usage is itemized separately from
# any other tooling. Set a hard spending limit on the key so a
# pathological tick can't drain the account.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model used for every tick. Pin a specific model ID rather than an
# alias so version drift doesn't surprise the harness. Defaults are
# nothing -- this must be set explicitly.
#
# Sensible choices:
#   claude-sonnet-4-6           # default working model -- balanced cost/capability
#   claude-opus-4-7             # premium -- complex reasoning, ambiguous tasks
#   claude-haiku-4-5-20251001   # cheap/fast -- light tasks only
IGOR_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6

# Optional. Model for in-harness "thinking" tasks (commit-subject
# derivation from diff, future classification/summarization helpers).
# These are single-shot API calls (no tool use, no agentic loop),
# so Haiku is the right default -- cheap and fast enough. Override
# only if you want Sonnet/Opus quality on these (rarely worth it).
# IGOR_MODEL_THINKING=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# Forgejo instance.
FORGEJO_URL=https://git.sherver.org

# Bot user's API token. The bot's identity is derived from this token
# (GET /api/v1/user). Required scopes:
#   read:user        -- whoami
#   write:repository -- repo content reads, PR listing/creation
#   write:issue      -- issue create/comment/label/assign/close
# (Forgejo splits repository and issue scopes -- you need both.)
# Push access for git is via the SSH key, separate from API scopes.
FORGEJO_TOKEN=

# Optional. SSH endpoint used for clone-on-demand. Defaults to the
# host extracted from FORGEJO_URL with port 22. Override if Forgejo
# SSH is on a non-default host or port. Format is "host" (port 22)
# or "host:port" (explicit). Examples:
#   FORGEJO_SSH_HOST=git.example.com           # port 22
#   FORGEJO_SSH_HOST=git.example.com:22381     # custom port
# FORGEJO_SSH_HOST=

# Optional. Per-tick Claude timeout (passed to `timeout`). Default 60m.
# IGOR_TIMEOUT=60m

# Optional. Where the harness keeps its state -- per-repo clones,
# per-tick worktrees, the global flock. Default ~/.local/state/igor.
# IGOR_STATE_DIR=

# Optional. How many days of commit history the RAG layer embeds per
# repo at the start of each tick (one of the three corpus sources --
# the others are brain/journal/ and brain/memories/). Default 30.
# Smaller = faster rebuild + smaller index; larger = more historical
# context retrievable.
# IGOR_RAG_COMMIT_DAYS=30

# Optional. Probability (0.0 to 1.0) that an empty tick (no claimable
# work) fires discretionary work (tier 2 maintenance, or tier 3 self-
# directed website). Default 0 (off). Bump to ~0.8 once you trust the
# loop. Bypassed entirely during Monday-morning maintenance windows --
# those fire every tick when there's a weekly-uncapped repo to audit.
# IGOR_DISCRETIONARY_RATE=0

# Optional. Forgejo username to assign each PR to for human review.
# When set, Igor opens PRs assigned to this user and processes any PRs
# that get reassigned back to him on subsequent ticks (the "assignment
# dance" -- review comments come in via reassignment, Igor addresses
# and reassigns back). Unset disables both halves.
# IGOR_REVIEWER=

# Optional shift window. When BOTH start and end are set (24h clock,
# local time), Igor only works ticks during [start, end). Outside the
# window, ticks exit immediately. Unset (default) means always-on --
# useful while dialing in. Posts on Igor's own blog are only attempted
# in the last hour of the shift (so site work happens first, post
# earns its place at end of day). When unconfigured, only the
# once-per-local-day cap gates posts. Example: 2am-6am every day:
# IGOR_SHIFT_START=2
# IGOR_SHIFT_END=6
